# sectop users and group (docs/architecture.md, Privilege split).
# install.sh installs this as /etc/sysusers.d/sectop.conf and adds one line:
#   m <admin user> sectop     (the UI reads /run/sectop, connects to the whois socket)
# sectop-feed: no members. The user helper's unit Group= and the collector's
# SupplementaryGroups=: the helper -> collector channel (/run/sectop-user/<user>/).
g sectop      -
g sectop-feed -
u sectop      -:sectop  "sectop collector"  -  -
u sectop-net  -:sectop  "sectop net unit"   -  -
